# Runtime secrets for `wrangler dev` / `pnpm cf:preview`.
# Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in. `.dev.vars` is gitignored; never commit it.
#
# Only server-read values belong here. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is inlined
# into the bundle by the Next compiler at build time, so it must be present in
# the environment that runs `pnpm cf:build` — putting it here is too late to
# have any effect. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Payment gateway (HitPay). Only needed when config/payments.yaml sets
# provider: hitpay. API key + webhook salt from the HitPay dashboard
# (Settings > API Keys), taken from the sandbox or production dashboard to
# match hitpay.environment in the config file.
HITPAY_API_KEY=
HITPAY_SALT=

# Transactional email. SMTP needs the Workers runtime for its socket, so
# `next dev` logs to the console regardless — use `pnpm cf:preview` to send.
# Under that runtime, leaving any of the three unset makes a send fail rather
# than log: on workerd a missing mailbox is a misconfiguration, not a fallback.
#
# Never rename these to NEXT_PUBLIC_*: the compiler would inline the password
# into the client bundle.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Defaults: 465, the SMTP_USER mailbox, "Startup Lab", 30000, 2.
# SMTP_REPLY_TO is omitted unless set — a reply address nobody reads is worse
# than none, so point it at a monitored mailbox or leave it blank.
# SMTP_PORT=
# SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=
# SMTP_FROM_NAME=
# SMTP_REPLY_TO=
# SMTP_TIMEOUT_MS=
# SMTP_ATTEMPTS=
